\ Protocol-bounded call site in interpreter-free AOT mode. The metadata-
\ only image still carries the protocol descriptor slot table, so the
\ satisfies-and-dispatch helper resolves the descriptor through the
\ slot table exactly as the runtime-image binary does -- with no
\ interpreter linked into the binary at all.
\
\ No bump-it method is registered for fixnum, so the check fails with a
\ protocol error and the binary exits with an error. The result is
\ dropped rather than printed: printing words still need interpreter
\ fallback, which the locked interpreter-free build rejects.

addable: protocol{ bump-it: } ;
bump-it: generic ( x: addable -- n ) [ drop 0 ] ;

\ Protocol-bounded call site: compiled output emits aotSatisfiesAndDispatch.
bounded-caller: ( x: addable -- n ) [ bump-it ] ;

1 bounded-caller drop
